{"type":"Film","id":"FR2014_031","slug":"fr2014-031-week-ends","title":{"native":"Week-ends","english":"Weekends in Normandy"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2014-02-26","year":2014},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Anne Villacèque","slug":"anne-villaceque","name":"Anne Villacèque","birthYear":1963,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Female identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]}],"genre":["Comedy","Drama"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/224/194/115424/format_page/week-ends.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W53G3TZD61U"},"synopsis":{"native":"Un rien suffit parfois à gâcher un week-end à la campagne. Un simple malentendu sur un parking de supermarché, un mauvais réflexe, et voilà que tout se détraque. Rien ne va plus pour Christine. Jean la quitte. Ses amis de toujours, Sylvette et Ulrich, sont un peu moins ses amis. Tout fout le camp. Mais la vie est toujours pleine de surprises. Amours et désamours dans la vie de deux couples, le temps des week-ends.","english":"It sometimes takes little to spoil a weekend in the country. A simple misunderstanding in a supermarket parking lot, a bad reaction, and there you go, everything is awry. Nothing is going well for Christine. Jean leaves her. Her oldest friends, Sylvette and Ulrich, are no longer such good friends. Everything is falling apart at the seams. But life is always full of surprises. Two couples, their passion and clashes, over a few weekends."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"FR2014_031_01","film":"FR2014_031","person":{"id":"Jacques Gamblin","slug":"jacques-gamblin","name":"Jacques Gamblin","birthYear":1957,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"age":"2: Late Middle Age (55-60)","gender":"Male identifying","sexuality":"Heterosexual","origin":"White Western European","class":"Middle class","profession":"Employed","ability":"Able-bodied","assistedMobil